BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventdiscoveringcharlescarrollofcarrolltonday25325-20261024@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261024T135628Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
SUMMARY:Discovering Charles Carroll of Carrollton Day
DESCRIPTION:No signers of the Declaration of Independence were born in Frederick County\, but a piece of our community is nonetheless inscribed on the founding document of our nation! As we mark the 250th Anniversary of the United States in 2026\, Heritage Frederick invites you to spend a day exploring Carrollton Manor on Saturday\, October 24\, 2026. Discover the history of Charles Carroll of Carrollton and the role his family played in overseeing Carrollton Manor in southeastern Frederick County. Learn about the many people that have inhabited and worked on the Manor throughout its history. Explore the legacy of this “unjustly neglected” Founder\, the only Catholic signer of the Declaration of Independence\, and his connections to Frederick County. Heritage Frederick and partner organizations are excited to invite you to a full day of programs\, informative displays\, and tours on October 24th. Our host location is Saint Joseph’s on Carrollton Manor Catholic Church\, located at 5843 Manor Woods Road\, Frederick\, MD 21703. Our exhibition hall at Saint Joseph’s will open at 9:00 am with displays provided by: Heritage Frederick Carroll County Farm Museum The National Shrine of Saint Elizabeth Ann Seton / Daughters of Charity Provincial Archives National Museum of Railroad History and Innovation Displays will feature historical and representative artifacts plus an opportunity to learn from knowledgeable guides covering various topics associated with Carrollton Manor’s history. The exhibit hall will be open from 9am until 3pm. Guided tours of the historic Saint Joseph on Carrollton Manor Catholic Church and Graveyard will be offered throughout the day. Built in 1822 and expanded to its present size in 1867\, Saint Joseph’s Church has recently been restored. Heritage Frederick will also unveil a new driving tour of Carrollton Manor which will help you explore this storied corner of Frederick County and the many diverse experiences that contribute to its history. Guides will be available at select sites to help you dive further into Carrollton Manor’s history. Food trucks will be at Saint Joseph’s on Carrollton Manor Church from 11am to 2pm to provide lunch and restrooms will be available at the Church. Support for this event has been generously provided by Frederick County's US Semiquincentennial Commission
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/discovering-charles-carroll-of-carrollton-day/25325/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
